                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel I waited a really long time for this game only to be terribly unimpressed by the result. \n\nGuards must be assassinated at a distance that is pixels away from bumping into them, which alerts them and instantly flips them around. \n\nHowever, if after shooting the guards shield a few times to distract him before running away, you manage to hide, don't worry. As long as he didn't die, he''ll return to his post and the alarm level will remain at 0.\n\nThe english translation is also painful at best. Tooltips and information are usually discernable, but you can't help but hear \"All your base are belong to us\" in the back of your mind as you scramble around the first few levels desperately trying to get a clue what is going on. The tutorial does a really good job of making you think it will give you everything you need to know to play the game, and then dumps you off at the central hub with too many options and no explanation.\n\nAll in all, I think this game still needs a lot of work before it is saleable, and I think Early Access at this point may prove to have been a bad idea.",
